  "body": "This PR defines a `privacy-policy` link type that refers to a document which\ncontains information about the data collection and usage practices that apply\nto the current context.\n\nThis link type was defined in [section 4 of RFC6903][1], and rediscovered in\na discussion at https://github.com/privacycg/proposals/issues/39.\n\n[1]: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6903#section-4\n\n---\n\nI'm submitting this as a PR, as there appears to be a reasonable amount of interest in the `privacy-policy` link type from the PrivacyCG discussion linked above. I haven't sent a similar PR for `terms-of-service` as it's not actually clear to me whether jumping straight to HTML is justified. So, I figured I'd ask in the form of a PR. :)\n\n- [X] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium (at least Chrome (👋)and Brave (@kdenhartog in [this comment](https://github.com/privacycg/proposals/issues/39#issuecomment-1707283509))).\n   * Gecko (@bvandersloot-mozilla's [last comment](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9860#issuecomment-1779233658) is supportive of the link type)\n- [X] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are unnecessary(?), as I don't think there's any web-facing mechanism of determining which link types a given user agent supports, nor is there any web-facing result of defining such a link type that's expected. See also @domenic's [comment below](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9860#pullrequestreview-1691711599) regarding `rel`'s supported tokens.\n- [X] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are unnecessary for the same reason.\n- [X] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/29801\n- [X] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9860/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 6, 2023, 8:33 AM UTC (1012ef3)\">/index.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9860/ce23076...1012ef3/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 6, 2023, 8:33 AM UTC (1012ef3)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9860/links.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 6, 2023, 8:33 AM UTC (1012ef3)\">/links.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9860/ce23076...1012ef3/links.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 6, 2023, 8:33 AM UTC (1012ef3)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9860/references.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 6, 2023, 8:33 AM UTC (1012ef3)\">/references.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9860/ce23076...1012ef3/references.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 6, 2023, 8:33 AM UTC (1012ef3)\">diff</a> )",
